Hey guys....(whisper, squeak).....

It is possible to run nethack with two floppies but you'll need 1 Meg of
RAM. Okay, here's the setup (I'm using DOS 3.3)...

A: (720K Floppy Drive)
 command.com + 2 hidden files. (I'd made the disk bootable).
 config.sys 	( just device= b:\ansi.sys & b:\vdisk.sys /360 /e)
 autoexec.bat	( optional )
 nethack.cnf	( use the given two floppy cfg. and 'save=b:\;n' )
		( Don't forget the 'ramdisk=c:\' )
 nethack.exe 	( compressed - read below for more info.)
 nethack1.ovl
 nethack2.ovl
B: (360K Floppy Drive)
 ansi.sys
 vdisk.sys
 (all the other nethack files goes here)
C: (Ramdisk of size 360K in extended memory)


TO COMPRESS NETHACK.EXE:
use FTP to secure the file lzexe91e.zip from 
 wuarchive.wuslt.edu site, it is in /mirrors/msdos/filutl/
 wsmr-simtel20.army.mil site, it is in pd1:<msdos.filutl>
 (Remember to specify 'tenex' before download in simtel20.)

Unzip the file and type 'lzexe nethack.exe'. Be sure that you're doing this
from the 720K floppy that has about 150K free AFTER nethack.exe is copied to
that floppy. It will compress nethack to about 107K.

NOTE: You can also use pklite.exe from /mirrors/msdos/arc-lbr/pk???.zip.
      (Check the index there). Both will provide the same compressed size.
      pk/unzip.eze can be found in /mirrors/msdos/arc-lbr/ directory.

The next step is to create a clean boot disk, create the config,sys file,
edit the nethack.cnf file, copy the nethack.exe file and uncompress the
overlay files. ( Having a RAMDISK is sure handy! )

I guess that you could use 640K but you'll need two 720K drives and it 
would be painfully slow. A cache program might provide some help.

I'm uncertain how large the .SAV file would be. When I last saved my 
endgame, it was at 330K. So, I guess it is 'safe' to store files in 
the 360K floppy. Could someone help me out? Thanx.

